  "description" : "<notes xmlns=\"http://www.sbml.org/sbml/level2\">      <body xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml\">        <p>Model reproduces the various plots in Figure 6 and 7 of the paper. It was successfully tested on MathSBML.</p>            <br />            <p>To the extent possible under law, all copyright and related or neighbouring rights to this encoded model have been dedicated to the public domain worldwide. Please refer to      <a href=\"http://creativecommons.org/publicdomain/zero/1.0/\" title=\"Creative Commons CC0\">CC0 Public Domain Dedication</a>          for more information.      </p>            <p>In summary, you are entitled to use this encoded model in absolutely any manner you deem suitable, verbatim, or with modification, alone or embedded it in a larger context, redistribute it, commercially or not, in a restricted way or not.</p>            <br />            <p>To cite BioModels Database, please use:      <a href=\"http://www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/pubmed/20587024\" target=\"_blank\">Li C, Donizelli M, Rodriguez N, Dharuri H, Endler L, Chelliah V, Li L, He E, Henry A, Stefan MI, Snoep JL, Hucka M, Le Novère N, Laibe C (2010) BioModels Database: An enhanced, curated and annotated resource for published quantitative kinetic models. BMC Syst Biol., 4:92.</a>                </p>            </body>          </notes>",
